# Next.js Folder Structure (ah-delights)

Use the App Router with a `src/` directory. Prefer colocated route code; keep shared code outside `app/`.

## Canonical layout

```
src/
  app/                    # Routes only (layouts, pages, route handlers, loading/error)
    (marketing)/          # Route groups for layout/URL organization (optional)
    api/                  # Route handlers → src/app/api/**/route.ts
    layout.tsx
    page.tsx
    globals.css
  components/
    ui/                   # Primitive/reusable UI (buttons, inputs, etc.)
    # Feature-named folders for composed UI (e.g. components/cart/)
  features/               # Domain modules (hooks, server actions, feature components)
  lib/                    # Shared utilities, clients, config helpers
  hooks/                  # Shared hooks used across features
  types/                  # Shared TypeScript types
  styles/                 # Global/non-route styles (if not in app/)
public/                   # Static assets only
```

## Placement rules

- **Routes live in `src/app/`** — only Next.js special files (`page`, `layout`, `loading`, `error`, `not-found`, `route`, `template`, `default`) and route-local `_components` / `_lib` when truly private to that segment.
- **No business logic dumping ground in `app/`** — put domain logic in `src/features/<name>/`, shared helpers in `src/lib/`.
- **Components**
  - Cross-cutting UI → `src/components/ui/`
  - Feature-specific UI → `src/features/<name>/components/` (or `src/components/<name>/` if thin)
- **Server actions / data access** → colocate under the owning feature (`src/features/<name>/`), not as loose files in `app/`.
- **Imports** — use the `@/` alias mapped to `src/` (e.g. `@/components/ui/button`, `@/features/cart`).
- **Do not** create a parallel root-level `app/` or `pages/` directory; do not put source outside `src/` except `public/`, config, and project root tooling.

## Examples

```text
✅ src/app/(shop)/products/[slug]/page.tsx
✅ src/features/products/get-product.ts
✅ src/components/ui/button.tsx

❌ app/page.tsx                          # wrong: missing src/
❌ src/app/utils/formatPrice.ts          # wrong: shared util belongs in lib/ or features/
❌ src/components/ProductCheckoutForm.tsx # prefer features/checkout/components/
```

When adding files, match this layout. If unsure, prefer `features/` for domain code and `components/ui/` for primitives.
